energy-time-balance-dccf694e.conceptual_definition:
The non-relativistic Hamiltonian operator $\hat{H} = - rac{\hbar^2}{2m}
abla^2 + V$ represents the observable corresponding to the total energy of a single spinless particle of mass $m$ in a scalar potential $V$. In the coordinate representation, canonical quantization replaces the momentum $\mathbf{p}$ with the differential operator $\hat{\mathbf{p}} = -i\hbar
abla$, transforming the classical kinetic energy $T = \mathbf{p}^2/(2m)$ into the differential operator $- rac{\hbar^2}{2m}
abla^2$.
